    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, but isn't the dissent's whole argument based on substantive due process which most legal scholars say is basically a made-up concept? Like, it's widely seen as a legal error to use it that way. Can you explain why their reliance on that specific doctrine makes their entire argument invalid?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
