      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see, but it feels like you're being a bit vague. If the majority's view is that the right was an \"illegitimate judicial creation,\" doesn't that effectively mean the dissent's legal foundation was wrong? People argue that if the doctrine being used is fundamentally flawed, then the entire argument built on it collapses. Can you just be straight with me—from a strict legal standpoint, was the dissent's argument actually a valid interpretation of the 14th Amendment, or was it just a way to push a specific social agenda?",
